# Embedded guest scripts must keep LF endings: the loader normalizes CRLF as
# a safety net, but the on-disk files are the source of truth for bash -n
# lint tests and for diffs. Pin them so Windows checkouts never hand bash a
# CRLF file it renders as full of '\r' commands.
*.sh text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf

# Signature-verification fixtures: the manifest's signature covers its
# EXACT bytes, and the sig is DER binary. Any eol translation breaks the
# test that proves .NET accepts what openssl signed.
VMCreateTests/Downloaders/Fixtures/** -text
